      "zh": "所当行的就是这样：要将一切男子和已嫁的女子尽行杀戮。」",
      "en": "Do this:[NOTE:1] Exterminate every male, as well as every woman who has experienced a man’s bed.[NOTE:2] But spare the lives of any virgins.” So they did as instructed.[NOTE:3]",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “And this is the thing that you will do.”",
        "Heb “a knower of the bed of a male.” The verb יָדָע (yadaʿ) “to know,” “be intimate with,” is used as a euphemism for sexual relations.",
        "Some Greek witnesses (notably Codex Vaticanus [B]) add the words, “‘But the virgins you should keep alive.’ And they did so.” These additional words, which probably represent the original Hebrew text, can be retroverted: וְאֶת־הַבְּתוּלוֹת תְּחַיּוּ וַיַּעֲשׂוּ כֵן (veʾet habbetulot tekhayyu vayyaʿasu khen). It is likely that a scribe’s eye jumped from the ו (vav) on וְאֶת (veʾet) to the initial vav of v. 11, accidentally leaving out the intervening letters. The present translation is based on this reconstruction."
      ],
